B.eSW=new A.y("Movement","The chest muscles push your arms forward, like when you push a door.")
B.eNH=new A.y("Movement","The biceps bends your elbow. When a muscle works it gets shorter and fatter.")
B.eRA=new A.y("Movement","The triceps straightens your elbow. It works opposite the biceps: muscles can only pull, so they come in pairs.")
B.eY7=new A.y("Movement","Long muscles in your forearm pull on tendons that work your fingers, like puppet strings.")
B.f40=new A.y("Movement","Your tummy muscles hold your body upright and help you bend and twist.")
B.f8a=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the sides of your waist that help you twist and lean.")
B.f0y=new A.y("Movement","The widest muscle in your back. It pulls your arms down, like when you swim or climb.")
B.eIR=new A.y("Movement","Your bottom muscles are the biggest in your body. They push you up stairs and keep you standing.")
B.eYj=new A.y("Movement","Four muscles at the front of your thigh. Together they are the strongest in your body for lifting weight.")
B.eJL=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the back of your thigh that bend your knee when you run.")
B.f4g=new A.y("Movement","The calf muscle pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.")
B.f5p=new A.y("Movement","These lift your foot up so your toes do not drag on the ground.")
B.eYL=new A.y("Nerves","Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells and runs everything you do.")
B.f4v=new A.y("Hormones","A butterfly-shaped gland in your neck. It makes hormones that control how fast your body uses energy.")
B.eL0=new A.y("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.f62=new A.y("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.eP8=new A.y("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.f3D=new A.y("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.eSA=new A.y("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.eWq=new A.y("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.f0U=new A.y("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.f6c=new A.y("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.f64=new A.y("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.f68=new A.y("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.eWZ=new A.y("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
B.f1S=new A.y("Digestion","About 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. This is where most food is turned into energy for your blood.")
B.f34=new A.y("Digestion","Takes the water from what is left and makes the rest into waste. It is about 1.5 metres long.")
B.f5P=new A.y("Cleaning","A stretchy bag that holds urine. It can hold about half a litre.")
B.eYK=new A.y("Nerves","A thick rope of nerves inside your backbone. It carries messages between your brain and the rest of your body.")
B.eUF=new A.y("Frame","Your skull is made of 22 bones that protect your brain. Only the jaw can move.")
